IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cp1-nouns`
IMPORT `cp1-amount-helpers`

-- Canada Pension Plan Act, Part I, Division A -- sections 8 and 9: CONTRIBUTIONS BY EMPLOYEES AND EMPLOYERS.
--
-- An employee contributes by deduction from remuneration, in three tiers: the base contribution (every year), the
-- first additional contribution (2019 on) and the second additional contribution (2024 on). An employer contributes
-- the same three tiers, in respect of each employee. Subsection 8(2) says when the deductions exceed what was
-- due (an excess amount) and subsection 8(3) how much of that is an overpayment under this Act; subsections 8(4)
-- to (11) prorate the exemption and the maximums when the employee has several employments.
--
-- Each rate, each maximum and the exemption is defined elsewhere (sections 11.1 to 20, in sibling modules of this
-- piece, and the Regulations, piece cr1). A rule here takes the figure as a plain NUMBER named as the text names
-- it, so a reader can set the rule beside the subsection. The seat layer (cp1-seat.l4) is what chains the sections.
--
-- out of range: Schedule 1 and Schedule 2 (piece cp6): the contribution rates for employees and employers.
-- out of range: regulation 5(5) (piece cr1): the amount prescribed as or on account of the basic exemption, per pay period.
-- out of range: regulation 6 (piece cr1) and a provincial pension plan: the amount "determined in the prescribed manner" to be the salary and wages on which a provincial contribution was made.
-- out of range: section 21 (piece cp2): the amounts the employer deducts from remuneration (the aggregates of subsection 8(2)).
--
-- A NUMBER result is the amount in dollars, worked out exactly as the subsection words it. The subsections have no
-- floor: wages below the exemption give a negative figure; see NOTES.md, "What the text turns out to say".
-- A MAYBE result is NOTHING where the paragraph does not apply to the year (before 2019 or 2024) or, in
-- subsections 8(2) to (11), where the ratio they prorate by cannot be formed (the employee has no wages at all).

§ `Division A -- Contributions Payable`

§§ `Section 8 -- the employee's contributions`

-- src:173 | Employee’s base contribution
-- src:174 | 8 (1) Every employee who is employed by an employer in pensionable employment shall, by deduction as provided in this Act from the remuneration in respect of the pensionable employment paid to the employee by the employer, make an employee’s base contribution for the year in which the remuneration is paid to the employee of an amount equal to the product obtained when the contribution rate for employees for the year is multiplied by the lesser of
-- src:175 | (a) the employee’s contributory salary and wages for the year paid by the employer, minus such amount as or on account of the basic exemption for the year as is prescribed, and
-- src:176 | (b) the employee’s maximum contributory earnings for the year, minus the amount, if any, that is determined in the prescribed manner to be the employee’s salary and wages paid by the employer on which a base contribution has been made for the year by the employee under a provincial pension plan.
@ref Act s 8(1) (src:173-176)
GIVEN `the contribution rate for employees for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the employee's contributory salary and wages for the year paid by the employer` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount prescribed as or on account of the basic exemption for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the employee's maximum contributory earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount, if any, determined in the prescribed manner to be the employee's salary and wages paid by the employer on which a base contribution has been made for the year by the employee under a provincial pension plan` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 8(1) — the employee's base contribution for the year`
        `the contribution rate for employees for the year`
        `the employee's contributory salary and wages for the year paid by the employer`
        `the amount prescribed as or on account of the basic exemption for the year`
        `the employee's maximum contributory earnings for the year`
        `the amount, if any, determined in the prescribed manner to be the employee's salary and wages paid by the employer on which a base contribution has been made for the year by the employee under a provincial pension plan`
    MEANS
        `the contribution rate for employees for the year`
        TIMES (min `paragraph (a)` `paragraph (b)`)
    WHERE
        -- (a) the employee's contributory salary and wages for the year paid by the employer, minus the prescribed exemption
        `paragraph (a)` MEANS
            `the employee's contributory salary and wages for the year paid by the employer` MINUS `the amount prescribed as or on account of the basic exemption for the year`
        -- (b) the employee's maximum contributory earnings for the year, minus the amount, if any, ... under a provincial pension plan
        `paragraph (b)` MEANS
            `the employee's maximum contributory earnings for the year` MINUS (fromMaybe 0 `the amount, if any, determined in the prescribed manner to be the employee's salary and wages paid by the employer on which a base contribution has been made for the year by the employee under a provincial pension plan`)

-- src:177 | Employee’s first additional contribution
-- src:178 | (1.1) For 2019 and each subsequent year, an employee referred to in subsection (1) shall also, by deduction as provided in this Act from the remuneration in respect of the pensionable employment paid to the employee by the employer, make an employee’s first additional contribution for the year in which the remuneration is paid to the employee of an amount equal to the product obtained when the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year is multiplied by the lesser of
-- src:179 | (a) the employee’s contributory salary and wages for the year paid by the employer, minus the amount as or on account of the basic exemption for the year that is prescribed, and
-- src:180 | (b) the employee’s maximum contributory earnings for the year, minus the amount, if any, that is determined in the prescribed manner to be the employee’s salary and wages paid by the employer on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year by the employee under a provincial pension plan.
@ref Act s 8(1.1) (src:177-180)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      `the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the employee's contributory salary and wages for the year paid by the employer` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount prescribed as or on account of the basic exemption for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the employee's maximum contributory earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount, if any, determined in the prescribed manner to be the employee's salary and wages paid by the employer on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year by the employee under a provincial pension plan` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 8(1.1) — the employee's first additional contribution for the year`
        year
        `the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year`
        `the employee's contributory salary and wages for the year paid by the employer`
        `the amount prescribed as or on account of the basic exemption for the year`
        `the employee's maximum contributory earnings for the year`
        `the amount, if any, determined in the prescribed manner to be the employee's salary and wages paid by the employer on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year by the employee under a provincial pension plan`
    MEANS
        -- "For 2019 and each subsequent year"
        IF year AT LEAST 2019
        THEN JUST (`the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year` TIMES (min `paragraph (a)` `paragraph (b)`))
        ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `paragraph (a)` MEANS
            `the employee's contributory salary and wages for the year paid by the employer` MINUS `the amount prescribed as or on account of the basic exemption for the year`
        `paragraph (b)` MEANS
            `the employee's maximum contributory earnings for the year` MINUS (fromMaybe 0 `the amount, if any, determined in the prescribed manner to be the employee's salary and wages paid by the employer on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year by the employee under a provincial pension plan`)

-- src:181 | Employee’s second additional contribution
-- src:182 | (1.2) For 2024 and each subsequent year, an employee referred to in subsection (1) shall also, by deduction as provided in this Act from the remuneration in respect of the pensionable employment paid to the employee by the employer, make an employee’s second additional contribution for the year in which the remuneration is paid to the employee of an amount equal to the product obtained when the second additional contribution rate for employees for the year is multiplied by the amount equal to
-- src:183 | (a) the amount by which the employee’s contributory salary and wages for the year paid by the employer — not exceeding the employee’s additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year — exceeds the employee’s maximum pensionable earnings for the year,
-- src:184 | minus
-- src:185 | (b) the amount, if any, that is determined in the prescribed manner to be the employee’s salary and wages paid by the employer on which a second additional contribution has been made for the year by the employee under a provincial pension plan.
@ref Act s 8(1.2) (src:181-185)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      `the second additional contribution rate for employees for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the employee's contributory salary and wages for the year paid by the employer` IS A NUMBER
      `the employee's additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the employee's maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount, if any, determined in the prescribed manner to be the employee's salary and wages paid by the employer on which a second additional contribution has been made for the year by the employee under a provincial pension plan` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 8(1.2) — the employee's second additional contribution for the year`
        year
        `the second additional contribution rate for employees for the year`
        `the employee's contributory salary and wages for the year paid by the employer`
        `the employee's additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year`
        `the employee's maximum pensionable earnings for the year`
        `the amount, if any, determined in the prescribed manner to be the employee's salary and wages paid by the employer on which a second additional contribution has been made for the year by the employee under a provincial pension plan`
    MEANS
        -- "For 2024 and each subsequent year"
        IF year AT LEAST 2024
        THEN JUST (`the second additional contribution rate for employees for the year` TIMES (`paragraph (a)` MINUS `paragraph (b)`))
        ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        -- (a) the amount by which the salary and wages -- not exceeding the additional maximum pensionable earnings -- exceed the maximum pensionable earnings
        `paragraph (a)` MEANS
            `the amount by which one amount exceeds another`
                (min `the employee's contributory salary and wages for the year paid by the employer` `the employee's additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year`)
                `the employee's maximum pensionable earnings for the year`
        -- (b) the amount, if any, ... under a provincial pension plan
        `paragraph (b)` MEANS
            fromMaybe 0 `the amount, if any, determined in the prescribed manner to be the employee's salary and wages paid by the employer on which a second additional contribution has been made for the year by the employee under a provincial pension plan`

-- Subsection 8(1.3) (Act line 186) reads "[Repealed, 2016, c. 14, s. 3]" in this text; there is nothing to encode (NOTES.md, coverage table).

§§ `Section 8(2) and (3) -- excess amount and overpayment`

-- The employee's own wages, in two groups: employments to which this Act's contribution provisions apply, and
-- employments to which a provincial pension plan applies. Not provisions: arithmetic over the employments.
GIVEN employments IS A LIST OF `cp1 Employment of an employee in a year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the contributory salary and wages from the employments to which the provisions of this Act relating to the making of contributions apply` employments MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN employment YIELD employment's `contributory salary and wages of the employee from the employment`)
             (filter (GIVEN employment YIELD employment's `the provisions of this Act relating to the making of contributions apply to the employment`) employments))

GIVEN employments IS A LIST OF `cp1 Employment of an employee in a year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the contributory salary and wages from the employments to which the provisions of a provincial pension plan apply` employments MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN employment YIELD employment's `contributory salary and wages of the employee from the employment`)
             (filter (GIVEN employment YIELD employment's `the provisions of a provincial pension plan apply to the employment`) employments))

-- src:213 | Prorated portion of employee’s basic exemption
-- src:214 | (4) For the purposes of subparagraphs (2)(a)(i) and (a.1)(i), the prorated portion of the employee’s basic exemption for the year is the product obtained when the employee’s basic exemption is multiplied by the ratio that
-- src:215 | (a) the employee’s contributory salary and wages for the year in respect of pensionable employment to which the provisions of this Act relating to the making of contributions apply, subject to
-- src:216 | (i) for each year before 2024, the maximum pensionable earnings in respect of each pensionable employment, and
-- src:217 | (ii) for 2024 and each subsequent year, the additional maximum pensionable earnings in respect of each pensionable employment,
-- src:218 | bears to
-- src:219 | (b) the aggregate of the employee’s contributory salary and wages for the year in respect of pensionable employment to which the provisions of this Act relating to the making of contributions apply or to which the provisions of a provincial pension plan apply, subject to
-- src:220 | (i) for each year before 2024, the maximum pensionable earnings in respect of each pensionable employment, and
-- src:221 | (ii) for 2024 and each subsequent year, the additional maximum pensionable earnings in respect of each pensionable employment.
-- (4)(a) bears to (b): the salary and wages of the employments to which this Act's contribution provisions apply, over those of
-- the employments to which this Act's or a provincial plan's provisions apply, each employment "subject to" the maximum
-- pensionable earnings (before 2024) or the additional maximum pensionable earnings (2024 on).
-- Not a provision of its own: the ratio that subsections (4), (5), (8) and (9) share.
GIVEN cap IS A NUMBER
      employments IS A LIST OF `cp1 Employment of an employee in a year`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the ratio of the capped salary and wages under this Act to the capped salary and wages under this Act or a provincial pension plan` cap employments MEANS
    IF `aggregate of both` EQUALS 0
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`aggregate under this Act` DIVIDED BY `aggregate of both`)
    WHERE
        `aggregate under this Act` MEANS
            sum (map (GIVEN employment YIELD min (employment's `contributory salary and wages of the employee from the employment`) cap)
                     (filter (GIVEN employment YIELD employment's `the provisions of this Act relating to the making of contributions apply to the employment`) employments))
        `aggregate of both` MEANS
            sum (map (GIVEN employment YIELD min (employment's `contributory salary and wages of the employee from the employment`) cap)
                     (filter (GIVEN employment YIELD (   employment's `the provisions of this Act relating to the making of contributions apply to the employment`
                                                     OR employment's `the provisions of a provincial pension plan apply to the employment`)) employments))

@ref Act s 8(4) (src:215-221)
GIVEN facts IS A `cp1 Facts about the contributions of an employee for a year`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 8(4) — the ratio of the salary and wages under this Act to the aggregate, before 2024 limited by the maximum pensionable earnings and from 2024 by the additional maximum pensionable earnings` facts MEANS
    `the ratio of the capped salary and wages under this Act to the capped salary and wages under this Act or a provincial pension plan`
        (IF facts's `the year at hand` LESS THAN 2024
         THEN facts's `the employee's maximum pensionable earnings for the year`
         ELSE facts's `the employee's additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year`)
        (facts's `employments of the employee in the year`)

@ref Act s 8(4) (src:213-214)
GIVEN `the employee's basic exemption` IS A NUMBER
      ratio IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 8(4) — the prorated portion of the employee's basic exemption` `the employee's basic exemption` ratio MEANS
    `the employee's basic exemption` TIMES ratio

