-- Subsection 8(2) adds the amounts of paragraphs (a) to (d). The record carries them, a paragraph that does not
-- apply to the year being NOTHING.
DECLARE `cp1 Amounts determined under subsection 8(2)` HAS
    `amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(a)` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(a.1)` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(a.2)` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(b)` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(c)` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(d)` IS A MAYBE NUMBER

-- Not a provision: the six paragraphs of subsection 8(2) worked out from one set of facts and the two ratios.
GIVEN facts IS A `cp1 Facts about the contributions of an employee for a year`
      `ratio under subsection (4)` IS A NUMBER
      `ratio under subsection (8)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `cp1 Amounts determined under subsection 8(2)`
`the amounts determined under the paragraphs of subsection 8(2)` facts `ratio under subsection (4)` `ratio under subsection (8)` MEANS
    `cp1 Amounts determined under subsection 8(2)` WITH
        `amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(a)` IS JUST `paragraph (a)`
        `amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(a.1)` IS `paragraph (a.1)`
        `amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(a.2)` IS `paragraph (a.2)`
        `amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(b)` IS JUST `paragraph (b)`
        `amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(c)` IS `paragraph (c)`
        `amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(d)` IS `paragraph (d)`
    WHERE
        `paragraph (a)` MEANS
            `s 8(2)(a) — the product of the contribution rate for employees under this Act and the lesser of the two amounts`
                (facts's `the contribution rate for employees for the year under this Act`)
                `wages under this Act`
                (facts's `contributory self-employed earnings of the employee for the year, if the employee is an individual described in section 10 to whom the provisions relating to the making of contributions apply`)
                `prorated basic exemption under (4)`
                `prorated maximum contributory earnings under (5)`
        `paragraph (a.1)` MEANS
            `s 8(2)(a.1) — the product of the first additional contribution rate for employees under this Act and the lesser of the two amounts`
                (facts's `the year at hand`)
                (facts's `the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year under this Act`)
                `wages under this Act`
                (facts's `contributory self-employed earnings of the employee for the year, if the employee is an individual described in section 10 to whom the provisions relating to the making of contributions apply`)
                `prorated basic exemption under (4)`
                `prorated maximum contributory earnings under (5)`
        `paragraph (a.2)` MEANS
            `s 8(2)(a.2) — the product of the second additional contribution rate for employees under this Act and the amount by which the earnings, not exceeding the prorated additional maximum, exceed the prorated maximum`
                (facts's `the year at hand`)
                (facts's `the second additional contribution rate for employees for the year under this Act`)
                `wages under this Act`
                (facts's `contributory self-employed earnings of the employee for the year, if the employee is an individual described in section 10 to whom the provisions relating to the making of contributions apply`)
                `prorated additional maximum under (8)`
                `prorated maximum under (9)`
        `paragraph (b)` MEANS
            `s 8(2)(b) — the product of the base contribution rate for employees under a provincial pension plan and the lesser of the two amounts`
                (facts's `the base contribution rate for employees for the year under a provincial pension plan`)
                `wages under a provincial pension plan`
                `prorated basic exemption under (6)`
                `prorated maximum contributory earnings under (7)`
        `paragraph (c)` MEANS
            `s 8(2)(c) — the product of the first additional contribution rate for employees under a provincial pension plan and the lesser of the two amounts`
                (facts's `the year at hand`)
                (facts's `the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year under a provincial pension plan`)
                `wages under a provincial pension plan`
                `prorated basic exemption under (6)`
                `prorated maximum contributory earnings under (7)`
        `paragraph (d)` MEANS
            `s 8(2)(d) — the product of the second additional contribution rate for employees under a provincial pension plan and the amount by which the wages, not exceeding the prorated additional maximum, exceed the prorated maximum`
                (facts's `the year at hand`)
                (facts's `the second additional contribution rate for employees for the year under a provincial pension plan`)
                `wages under a provincial pension plan`
                `prorated additional maximum under (10)`
                `prorated maximum under (11)`
        `wages under this Act` MEANS
            `the contributory salary and wages from the employments to which the provisions of this Act relating to the making of contributions apply` (facts's `employments of the employee in the year`)
        `wages under a provincial pension plan` MEANS
            `the contributory salary and wages from the employments to which the provisions of a provincial pension plan apply` (facts's `employments of the employee in the year`)
        `prorated basic exemption under (4)` MEANS
            `s 8(4) — the prorated portion of the employee's basic exemption` (facts's `the employee's basic exemption for the year`) `ratio under subsection (4)`
        `prorated maximum contributory earnings under (5)` MEANS
            `s 8(5) — the prorated portion of the employee's maximum contributory earnings` (facts's `the employee's maximum contributory earnings for the year`) `ratio under subsection (4)`
        `prorated basic exemption under (6)` MEANS
            `s 8(6) — the prorated portion of the employee's basic exemption for a provincial pension plan`
                (facts's `the employee's basic exemption for the year, determined without taking into account paragraphs 19(b) and (c)`)
                `prorated basic exemption under (4)`
        `prorated maximum contributory earnings under (7)` MEANS
            `s 8(7) — the prorated portion of the employee's maximum contributory earnings for a provincial pension plan`
                (facts's `the employee's maximum contributory earnings for the year, determined without taking into account paragraphs 17(b) and (c) and 19(b) and (c)`)
                `prorated maximum contributory earnings under (5)`
        `prorated additional maximum under (8)` MEANS
            `s 8(8) — the prorated portion of the employee's additional maximum pensionable earnings` (facts's `the employee's additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year`) `ratio under subsection (8)`
        `prorated maximum under (9)` MEANS
            `s 8(9) — the prorated portion of the employee's maximum pensionable earnings` (facts's `the employee's maximum pensionable earnings for the year`) `ratio under subsection (8)`
        `prorated additional maximum under (10)` MEANS
            `s 8(10) — the prorated portion of the employee's additional maximum pensionable earnings for a provincial pension plan`
                (facts's `the employee's additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year, determined without taking into account paragraphs 17.1(b) and (c)`)
                `prorated additional maximum under (8)`
        `prorated maximum under (11)` MEANS
            `s 8(11) — the prorated portion of the employee's maximum pensionable earnings for a provincial pension plan`
                (facts's `the employee's maximum pensionable earnings for the year, determined without taking into account paragraphs 17(b) and (c)`)
                `prorated maximum under (9)`

-- The sum obtained by adding the amounts: a paragraph that does not apply to the year adds nothing.
GIVEN amounts IS A `cp1 Amounts determined under subsection 8(2)`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the sum of the amounts of paragraphs 8(2)(a) to (d)` amounts MEANS
        fromMaybe 0 (amounts's `amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(a)`)
    PLUS fromMaybe 0 (amounts's `amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(a.1)`)
    PLUS fromMaybe 0 (amounts's `amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(a.2)`)
    PLUS fromMaybe 0 (amounts's `amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(b)`)
    PLUS fromMaybe 0 (amounts's `amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(c)`)
    PLUS fromMaybe 0 (amounts's `amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(d)`)

-- The sum of the amounts of paragraphs 8(2)(a) to (a.2), which paragraph 8(3)(a) subtracts.
GIVEN amounts IS A `cp1 Amounts determined under subsection 8(2)`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the sum of the amounts of paragraphs 8(2)(a) to (a.2)` amounts MEANS
        fromMaybe 0 (amounts's `amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(a)`)
    PLUS fromMaybe 0 (amounts's `amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(a.1)`)
    PLUS fromMaybe 0 (amounts's `amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(a.2)`)

-- src:187 | Excess amount
-- src:188 | (2) An excess amount has been paid if the aggregate of all amounts deducted as required from the remuneration of an employee for a year, whether by one or more employers, on account of the employee’s contributions for the year under this Act or under a provincial pension plan exceeds the sum obtained by adding the following amounts:
@ref Act s 8(2) (src:187-188)
GIVEN facts IS A `cp1 Facts about the contributions of an employee for a year`
GIVETH A MAYBE `cp1 Amounts determined under subsection 8(2)`
`s 8(2) — the amounts determined under paragraphs (a) to (d)` facts MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 8(4) — the ratio of the salary and wages under this Act to the aggregate, before 2024 limited by the maximum pensionable earnings and from 2024 by the additional maximum pensionable earnings` facts
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST `ratio under subsection (4)` THEN
        CONSIDER `s 8(8) — the ratio of the salary and wages under this Act to the aggregate, each employment limited by the additional maximum pensionable earnings` facts
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST `ratio under subsection (8)` THEN
            JUST (`the amounts determined under the paragraphs of subsection 8(2)` facts `ratio under subsection (4)` `ratio under subsection (8)`)

@ref Act s 8(2) (src:187-188)
GIVEN facts IS A `cp1 Facts about the contributions of an employee for a year`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 8(2) — the excess amount calculated` facts MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 8(2) — the amounts determined under paragraphs (a) to (d)` facts
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST amounts THEN
        JUST ((facts's `aggregate of all amounts deducted as required from the remuneration of the employee for the year on account of the employee's contributions under this Act or under a provincial pension plan`)
              MINUS `the sum of the amounts of paragraphs 8(2)(a) to (d)` amounts)

@ref Act s 8(2) (src:187-188)
GIVEN facts IS A `cp1 Facts about the contributions of an employee for a year`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(2) — an excess amount has been paid` facts MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 8(2) — the excess amount calculated` facts
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST excess THEN JUST (excess GREATER THAN 0)

-- src:209 | Overpayment
-- src:210 | (3) The overpayment made by the employee on account of the employee’s contributions for the year under this Act is the lesser of
-- src:211 | (a) the aggregate of all amounts deducted as required from the remuneration of that employee on account of the employee’s contributions under this Act for the year, minus the sum of the amounts determined under paragraphs (2)(a) to (a.2), and
-- src:212 | (b) the excess amount calculated in accordance with subsection (2).
@ref Act s 8(3) (src:209-212)
GIVEN facts IS A `cp1 Facts about the contributions of an employee for a year`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 8(3) — the overpayment made by the employee on account of the employee's contributions under this Act` facts MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 8(2) — the amounts determined under paragraphs (a) to (d)` facts
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST amounts THEN
        CONSIDER `s 8(2) — the excess amount calculated` facts
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST excess THEN
            -- (a) the aggregate deducted under this Act, minus the sum of the amounts determined under paragraphs (2)(a) to (a.2); (b) the excess amount
            JUST (min
                      ((facts's `aggregate of all amounts deducted as required from the remuneration of the employee for the year on account of the employee's contributions under this Act`)
                       MINUS `the sum of the amounts of paragraphs 8(2)(a) to (a.2)` amounts)
                      excess)

§§ `Section 9 -- the employer's contributions`

-- src:249 | Employer’s base contribution
-- src:250 | 9 (1) Every employer shall, in respect of each employee employed by the employer in pensionable employment, make an employer’s base contribution for the year in which remuneration in respect of the pensionable employment is paid to the employee of an amount equal to the product obtained when the contribution rate for employers for the year is multiplied by the lesser of
-- src:251 | (a) the contributory salary and wages of the employee for the year paid by the employer, minus such amount as or on account of the employee’s basic exemption for the year as is prescribed, and
-- src:252 | (b) the maximum contributory earnings of the employee for the year, minus the amount, if any, that is determined in the prescribed manner to be the employee’s salary and wages on which a base contribution has been made for the year by the employer with respect to the employee under a provincial pension plan.
@ref Act s 9(1) (src:249-252)
GIVEN `the contribution rate for employers for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the contributory salary and wages of the employee for the year paid by the employer` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount prescribed as or on account of the employee's basic exemption for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum contributory earnings of the employee for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount, if any, determined in the prescribed manner to be the employee's salary and wages on which a base contribution has been made for the year by the employer with respect to the employee under a provincial pension plan` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 9(1) — the employer's base contribution for the year in respect of an employee`
        `the contribution rate for employers for the year`
        `the contributory salary and wages of the employee for the year paid by the employer`
        `the amount prescribed as or on account of the employee's basic exemption for the year`
        `the maximum contributory earnings of the employee for the year`
        `the amount, if any, determined in the prescribed manner to be the employee's salary and wages on which a base contribution has been made for the year by the employer with respect to the employee under a provincial pension plan`
    MEANS
        `the contribution rate for employers for the year`
        TIMES (min `paragraph (a)` `paragraph (b)`)
    WHERE
        `paragraph (a)` MEANS
            `the contributory salary and wages of the employee for the year paid by the employer` MINUS `the amount prescribed as or on account of the employee's basic exemption for the year`
        `paragraph (b)` MEANS
            `the maximum contributory earnings of the employee for the year` MINUS (fromMaybe 0 `the amount, if any, determined in the prescribed manner to be the employee's salary and wages on which a base contribution has been made for the year by the employer with respect to the employee under a provincial pension plan`)

-- src:253 | Employer’s first additional contribution
-- src:254 | (1.1) For 2019 and each subsequent year, an employer referred to in subsection (1) shall also, in respect of each employee employed by the employer in pensionable employment, make an employer’s first additional contribution for the year in which remuneration in respect of the pensionable employment is paid to the employee of an amount equal to the product obtained when the first additional contribution rate for employers for the year is multiplied by the lesser of
-- src:255 | (a) the employee’s contributory salary and wages for the year paid by the employer, minus the amount as or on account of the employee’s basic exemption for the year that is prescribed, and
-- src:256 | (b) the employee’s maximum contributory earnings for the year, minus the amount, if any, that is determined in the prescribed manner to be the employee’s salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year by the employer with respect to the employee under a provincial pension plan.
@ref Act s 9(1.1) (src:253-256)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      `the first additional contribution rate for employers for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the employee's contributory salary and wages for the year paid by the employer` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount prescribed as or on account of the employee's basic exemption for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the employee's maximum contributory earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount, if any, determined in the prescribed manner to be the employee's salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year by the employer with respect to the employee under a provincial pension plan` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 9(1.1) — the employer's first additional contribution for the year in respect of an employee`
        year
        `the first additional contribution rate for employers for the year`
        `the employee's contributory salary and wages for the year paid by the employer`
        `the amount prescribed as or on account of the employee's basic exemption for the year`
        `the employee's maximum contributory earnings for the year`
        `the amount, if any, determined in the prescribed manner to be the employee's salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year by the employer with respect to the employee under a provincial pension plan`
    MEANS
        -- "For 2019 and each subsequent year"
        IF year AT LEAST 2019
        THEN JUST (`the first additional contribution rate for employers for the year` TIMES (min `paragraph (a)` `paragraph (b)`))
        ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `paragraph (a)` MEANS
            `the employee's contributory salary and wages for the year paid by the employer` MINUS `the amount prescribed as or on account of the employee's basic exemption for the year`
        `paragraph (b)` MEANS
            `the employee's maximum contributory earnings for the year` MINUS (fromMaybe 0 `the amount, if any, determined in the prescribed manner to be the employee's salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year by the employer with respect to the employee under a provincial pension plan`)

-- src:257 | Employer’s second additional contribution
-- src:258 | (1.2) For 2024 and each subsequent year, an employer referred to in subsection (1) shall also, in respect of each employee employed by the employer in pensionable employment, make an employer’s second additional contribution for the year in which remuneration in respect of the pensionable employment is paid to the employee of an amount equal to the product obtained when the second additional contribution rate for employers for the year is multiplied by the amount equal to
-- src:259 | (a) the amount by which the employee’s contributory salary and wages for the year paid by the employer — not exceeding the employee’s additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year — exceeds the employee’s maximum pensionable earnings for the year,
-- src:260 | minus
-- src:261 | (b) the amount, if any, that is determined in the prescribed manner to be the employee’s salary and wages on which a second additional contribution has been made for the year by the employer with respect to the employee under a provincial pension plan.
@ref Act s 9(1.2) (src:257-261)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      `the second additional contribution rate for employers for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the employee's contributory salary and wages for the year paid by the employer` IS A NUMBER
      `the employee's additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the employee's maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount, if any, determined in the prescribed manner to be the employee's salary and wages on which a second additional contribution has been made for the year by the employer with respect to the employee under a provincial pension plan` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 9(1.2) — the employer's second additional contribution for the year in respect of an employee`
        year
        `the second additional contribution rate for employers for the year`
        `the employee's contributory salary and wages for the year paid by the employer`
        `the employee's additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year`
        `the employee's maximum pensionable earnings for the year`
        `the amount, if any, determined in the prescribed manner to be the employee's salary and wages on which a second additional contribution has been made for the year by the employer with respect to the employee under a provincial pension plan`
    MEANS
        -- "For 2024 and each subsequent year"
        IF year AT LEAST 2024
        THEN JUST (`the second additional contribution rate for employers for the year` TIMES (`paragraph (a)` MINUS `paragraph (b)`))
        ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `paragraph (a)` MEANS
            `the amount by which one amount exceeds another`
                (min `the employee's contributory salary and wages for the year paid by the employer` `the employee's additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year`)
                `the employee's maximum pensionable earnings for the year`
        `paragraph (b)` MEANS
            fromMaybe 0 `the amount, if any, determined in the prescribed manner to be the employee's salary and wages on which a second additional contribution has been made for the year by the employer with respect to the employee under a provincial pension plan`

§§ `Section 9(2) and (3) -- succession of employers; self-employment succeeded by employment`

-- src:262 | Succession of employers
-- src:263 | (2) If one employer immediately succeeds another as the employer of an employee as a result of the formation or dissolution of a corporation or the acquisition — with the agreement of the former employer or by operation of law — of all or part of a business of the former employer, the successor employer may, for the application of subsections (1), (1.1) and (1.2) and 8(1), (1.1) and (1.2) and section 21, take into account the amounts paid, deducted, remitted or contributed under this Act by the former employer in respect of the year in relation to the employment of the employee as if they had been paid, deducted, remitted or contributed by the successor employer. If the employer takes those amounts into account with respect to the employer’s contributions, the employer shall also take them into account with respect to the employee’s contributions.
-- The first sentence is a permission for the successor employer ("may"); the second a duty that follows when it
-- takes the amounts into account for its own contributions.
@ref Act s 9(2) (src:262-263)
GIVEN `the successor employer immediately succeeds the former employer as the employer of the employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the succession is a result of the formation or dissolution of a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the succession is a result of the acquisition of all or part of a business of the former employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the acquisition is with the agreement of the former employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the acquisition is by operation of law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 9(2) — the successor employer may take into account the amounts the former employer paid, deducted, remitted or contributed`
        `the successor employer immediately succeeds the former employer as the employer of the employee`
        `the succession is a result of the formation or dissolution of a corporation`
        `the succession is a result of the acquisition of all or part of a business of the former employer`
        `the acquisition is with the agreement of the former employer`
        `the acquisition is by operation of law`
    MEANS
            `the successor employer immediately succeeds the former employer as the employer of the employee`
        AND (    `the succession is a result of the formation or dissolution of a corporation`
              OR (    `the succession is a result of the acquisition of all or part of a business of the former employer`
                  AND (   `the acquisition is with the agreement of the former employer`
                       OR `the acquisition is by operation of law`)))

@ref Act s 9(2) (src:262-263)
GIVEN `the successor employer may take into account the amounts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amounts paid, deducted, remitted or contributed under this Act by the former employer in respect of the year in relation to the employment of the employee` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 9(2) — the amount the successor employer may take into account as if it had paid, deducted, remitted or contributed it`
        `the successor employer may take into account the amounts`
        `the amounts paid, deducted, remitted or contributed under this Act by the former employer in respect of the year in relation to the employment of the employee`
    MEANS
        IF `the successor employer may take into account the amounts`
        THEN JUST `the amounts paid, deducted, remitted or contributed under this Act by the former employer in respect of the year in relation to the employment of the employee`
        ELSE NOTHING

-- "If the employer takes those amounts into account with respect to the employer's contributions, the employer
-- shall also take them into account with respect to the employee's contributions."
@ref Act s 9(2) (src:263)
GIVEN `the successor employer takes the amounts into account with respect to the employer's contributions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 9(2) — the successor employer must also take the amounts into account with respect to the employee's contributions` `the successor employer takes the amounts into account with respect to the employer's contributions` MEANS
    `the successor employer takes the amounts into account with respect to the employer's contributions`

-- src:264 | Self-employment succeeded by employment
-- src:265 | (3) For the application of subsections (1), (1.1) and (1.2) and 8(1), (1.1) and (1.2) and section 21, if a person, in a year, is self-employed, ceases to be self-employed and becomes an employee of a corporation that is controlled by the person, the corporation may
-- src:266 | (a) take into account the amount of contributory self-employed earnings of the person in the year as contributory salary and wages paid by the corporation to the employee in that year; and
-- src:267 | (b) take into account one half of the contributions by the person in respect of self-employed earnings in the year as an amount deducted, remitted or contributed in relation to employee’s contributions for that year, and one half of that amount as an amount remitted or contributed in relation to employer’s contributions for that year.
@ref Act s 9(3) (src:264-265)
GIVEN `the person, in a year, is self-employed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person ceases to be self-employed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person becomes an employee of a corporation that is controlled by the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 9(3) — the corporation may take into account the person's self-employment` `the person, in a year, is self-employed` `the person ceases to be self-employed` `the person becomes an employee of a corporation that is controlled by the person` MEANS
        `the person, in a year, is self-employed`
    AND `the person ceases to be self-employed`
    AND `the person becomes an employee of a corporation that is controlled by the person`

@ref Act s 9(3)(a) (src:266)
GIVEN `the corporation may take into account the person's self-employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of contributory self-employed earnings of the person in the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 9(3)(a) — the amount the corporation may take into account as contributory salary and wages paid to the employee in that year` `the corporation may take into account the person's self-employment` `the amount of contributory self-employed earnings of the person in the year` MEANS
    IF `the corporation may take into account the person's self-employment`
    THEN JUST `the amount of contributory self-employed earnings of the person in the year`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Reading taken (NOTES.md, fork register): "one half of that amount" is one half of "the contributions by the person", so
-- the employee's side and the employer's side each take one half.
@ref Act s 9(3)(b) (src:267)
GIVEN `the corporation may take into account the person's self-employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contributions by the person in respect of self-employed earnings in the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 9(3)(b) — the amount the corporation may take into account in relation to the employee's contributions for that year` `the corporation may take into account the person's self-employment` `the contributions by the person in respect of self-employed earnings in the year` MEANS
    IF `the corporation may take into account the person's self-employment`
    THEN JUST (`the contributions by the person in respect of self-employed earnings in the year` DIVIDED BY 2)
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref Act s 9(3)(b) (src:267)
GIVEN `the corporation may take into account the person's self-employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contributions by the person in respect of self-employed earnings in the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 9(3)(b) — the amount the corporation may take into account in relation to the employer's contributions for that year` `the corporation may take into account the person's self-employment` `the contributions by the person in respect of self-employed earnings in the year` MEANS
    IF `the corporation may take into account the person's self-employment`
    THEN JUST (`the contributions by the person in respect of self-employed earnings in the year` DIVIDED BY 2)
    ELSE NOTHING
